<%#
  The step panel's Connections section, rendered on its own so a save that
  flips "Come back to this workflow" can re-render it in place
  (StepsController#update).

  Doors come first: the ways out of THIS step, worked out from the step
  itself (Step::Doors) and rendered whether or not anyone has wired them.
  Below that, "Other connections" is the editor, narrowed to the transitions
  Step::Doors did not claim — numeric ranges, other variables, anything a
  door does not describe.

  A handoff takes no doors: it ends this workflow by handing the run on, and
  the Sub-Flow fields say so right above. One that still carries a connection
  keeps the editor, or there would be no way to remove it.

  Local variables:
  - step: AR Step object
  - workflow: Workflow object
  - readonly: boolean (default false)
%>
<% readonly = local_assigns.fetch(:readonly, false) %>
<%= render "steps/doors", step: step, workflow: workflow, readonly: readonly %>
<% if !readonly && (!step.hands_off? || step.transitions.any?) %>
  <%= render "steps/transitions_editor", step: step, workflow: workflow %>
<% end %>
